OS 4.0
\ The disk misbehaving (V4): a disk that stops answering, then answers again.  ok
\ Its requests go to a queue the device was never given, so none completes.  ok
7 block drop  ok
data-disk @ disk d.vq @ constant real-vq  ok
8 new-vq constant dead-vq  ok
: deaf  ( -- )  dead-vq data-disk @ disk d.vq ! ;  ok
: hear  ( -- )  real-vq data-disk @ disk d.vq ! ;  ok
\ A read the disk never answers: -263, and no buffer claims the block.  ok
deaf  9 ' block catch .  drop  hear -263  ok
9 block c@ . 0  ok
\ A write the disk never answers: -263, and the change waits to be written.  ok
65 9 block c!  update  ok
deaf  ' save-buffers catch .  hear -263  ok
save-buffers  empty-buffers  9 block c@ . 65  ok
\ The queue record the proofs assume (BlkQueue in Drivers.lean): 8 entries,  ok
\ the descriptor table 40 to 55 bytes after the record, the available ring  ok
\ right after the table, and the queue apart from the disk's own record.  ok
real-vq vq-size . 8  ok
real-vq dup 2 cells + @ swap - 40 56 within . -1  ok
real-vq dup 3 cells + @ swap 2 cells + @ - . 128  ok
real-vq data-disk @ disk - 56 u< 0= .  data-disk @ disk real-vq - 204 u< 0= . -1 -1  ok
\ And the system carries on.  ok
2 3 + . 5  ok
